>
  <h1>Schemas &amp; Plugins</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Extend the VC SDK with domain-specific credential types. Plugins auto-inject
    JSON-LD contexts, map properties, and compose with each other.
  </p>

  <h2>SchemaPlugin interface</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="SchemaPlugin interface">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">interface</span> <span class="c-typ">SchemaPlugin</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  context: <span class="c-typ">string</span>                   <span class="c-cm">// JSON-LD @context URI to inject</span>
  types: <span class="c-typ">string</span>[]                   <span class="c-cm">// Credential types this plugin handles</span>
  propertyMap: <span class="c-typ">Record</span><span class="c-op">&lt;</span><span class="c-typ">string</span>, <span class="c-br">{</span>   <span class="c-cm">// Maps claim keys to JSON-LD terms</span>
    term: <span class="c-typ">string</span>
    type<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>
  <span class="c-br">}</span><span class="c-op">&gt;</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>How plugins work</h2>
  <p>When a schema plugin is registered and a credential is issued with a matching type:</p>

  <ol style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li>The plugin's <code>context</code> URI is added to the credential's <code>@context</code> array.</li>
    <li>Claims are wrapped according to the <code>propertyMap</code> — mapping your keys to JSON-LD terms.</li>
    <li>The credential type array is validated against the plugin's <code>types</code>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Registering plugins</h2>
  <p>Use <code>issuer.use()</code> to register plugins. Calls are chainable:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Plugin registration">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCIssuer, generateKeyPair <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>
<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> drivingLicenseSchema, medicalCertSchema <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>()

<span class="c-kw">const</span> issuer = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCIssuer</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  did: <span class="c-str">'did:web:issuer.example.com'</span>,
  privateKey: keys.privateKey,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)
  .<span class="c-fn">use</span>(drivingLicenseSchema)
  .<span class="c-fn">use</span>(medicalCertSchema)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Creating a custom plugin</h2>
  <p>Define your own schema for any credential type:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Custom schema plugin">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-kw">type</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> SchemaPlugin <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> employmentSchema<span class="c-op">:</span> <span class="c-typ">SchemaPlugin</span> = <span class="c-br">{</span>
  context: <span class="c-str">'https://schemas.example.com/employment/v1'</span>,
  types: [<span class="c-str">'EmploymentCredential'</span>],
  propertyMap: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    employer: <span class="c-br">{</span> term: <span class="c-str">'schema:employer'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span>,
    jobTitle: <span class="c-br">{</span> term: <span class="c-str">'schema:jobTitle'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span>,
    startDate: <span class="c-br">{</span> term: <span class="c-str">'schema:startDate'</span>, type: <span class="c-str">'xsd:date'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Using the custom plugin">
<Fragment set:html={`issuer.<span class="c-fn">use</span>(employmentSchema)

<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'EmploymentCredential'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:employee.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    employer: <span class="c-str">'Acme Corp'</span>,
    jobTitle: <span class="c-str">'Software Engineer'</span>,
    startDate: <span class="c-str">'2026-01-15'</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

<span class="c-cm">// vc['@context'] includes 'https://schemas.example.com/employment/v1'</span>
<span class="c-cm">// vc.type includes 'EmploymentCredential'</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Multiple plugins coexisting</h2>
  <p>
    Plugins are independent. Each one only activates when the issued credential's type
    matches its <code>types</code> array. Multiple plugins can be registered simultaneously:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Multiple plugins">
<Fragment set:html={`issuer
  .<span class="c-fn">use</span>(drivingLicenseSchema)     <span class="c-cm">// activates for 'DrivingLicense'</span>
  .<span class="c-fn">use</span>(medicalCertSchema)         <span class="c-cm">// activates for 'MedicalCertificate'</span>
  .<span class="c-fn">use</span>(employmentSchema)          <span class="c-cm">// activates for 'EmploymentCredential'</span>

<span class="c-cm">// Each issue() call triggers only the matching plugin</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> license = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span> type: <span class="c-str">'DrivingLicense'</span>, ... <span class="c-br">}</span>)
<span class="c-kw">const</span> medical = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span> type: <span class="c-str">'MedicalCertificate'</span>, ... <span class="c-br">}</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>Costa Rica schemas included.</strong> The <code>@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas</code>
    package provides ready-made plugins for Costa Rica credential types: driving licenses,
    medical certificates, vehicle inspections, and more.
    <a href="/docs/credentials/costa-rica/">See the full list.</a>
  </Callout>

